---
title: Inviting an employee by one-time link
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Owner
  participant App as Next.js app
  participant DB as Postgres
  actor Employee

  Owner->>App: Invite email + role (advisor, mechanic, inventory, cashier)
  App->>App: requirePermission("staff.manage")
  App->>DB: rpc create_invitation()
  Note over DB: Owner check · random 32-byte token · only its SHA-256 hash is stored ·<br/>older pending invite for that email revoked · activity logged
  DB-->>App: Raw token (returned once, never stored)
  App-->>Owner: Invite link with Copy and Share on WhatsApp
  Owner-->>Employee: Sends the link (WhatsApp or any channel)
  Employee->>App: Opens /invite/<token>
  App->>DB: rpc get_invitation(token)
  DB-->>App: Workshop name, role, invited email, status
  alt Not signed in
    Employee->>App: Register or log in with the invited email (next=/invite/<token>)
  end
  Employee->>App: Accept and join
  App->>DB: rpc accept_invitation(token)
  Note over DB: Valid, not expired, not revoked, email matches →<br/>membership with that role · invite marked used · activity logged
  App-->>Employee: Dashboard with the role's navigation
